<title>CANADA: CANADIAN NATIONAL TRAIN DERAILS IN SOUTH MANITOBA.</title>
<headline>CANADIAN NATIONAL TRAIN DERAILS IN SOUTH MANITOBA.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>A 23-car Canadian National Railway Co train carrying grain derailed Wednesday afternoon east of the southern Manitoba village of Kane, Royal Canadian Mounted Police said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Eight hopper cars jumped the tracks around 1615 CDT/2115 GMT but no one was injured, RCMP Const. Luc Gervais said.</p>
<p>CN officials were not immediately available for comment. It was not immediately known what type of grain or other goods the train was carrying.</p>
<p>The rail line is a secondary line from Elgin to Morris, Manitoba.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
